alpha) subunit. The gene is brain-specific, and located in the neocortex and the striatum. It may be involved in cellular excitability of restricted neurons in the central nervous system. [provided by RefSeq, Jul 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9UQ05","text":"Pore-forming (alpha) subunit of a voltage-gated delayed rectifier (PubMed:10455180). Activates at more negative voltages, exhibits fast prepulse-independent activation kinetics and deactivates much more slowly, but shows no inactivation (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}